From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Marko Saukko <marko.saukko@jolla.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Nov 2026 08:48:11 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Update operator APN settings from Android APN data. JB#66116

Update internet and MMS access points where the Android apns-conf.xml
shipped on a recent MediaTek device differs from ours and LineageOS or
the AOSP sample apns-full-conf.xml has the same settings. Only base
operator entries are used, not MVNO entries matched by GID or IMSI.

Settings changed by our earlier patches, XCAP, IMS, emergency and
Wi-Fi only access points, the protocol and proxy-only differences are
left as they are. An MMSC or proxy that is an IP address is not
replaced with a host name, and an internet access point is not
switched to one we already list for MMS or WAP.

When the access point name changes, take the username and password
from the Android entry and drop a display name based on the old one.
---
